.TH BATTERY-HEALTH-CENTER 1 "October 2026" "battery-health-center 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
battery-health-center \- battery health, charge limits and energy use in one place
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery-health-center
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.br
.B battery-health-center \-\-export\-report
.I FILE
.br
.B battery-health-center \-\-export\-csv
.I FOLDER
.SH DESCRIPTION
A GNOME application showing the health of the laptop battery (maximum capacity,
condition, cycle count), the charger, battery use during sleep and which
applications use the most energy.
It can limit how far the battery charges (with presets), charge it to 100% once
or on a schedule, switch the power mode automatically, and change GNOME's
power-saving settings.
.PP
Changing the charge limit asks for a password through PolicyKit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without a window, so that battery history keeps being recorded.
The Usage page can start the application this way at login.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-report " FILE"
Write an HTML battery report to
.I FILE
and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-csv " FOLDER"
Write the recorded history as four CSV files (battery level and power, capacity over time, sleep sessions, per\-app energy use) into
.I FOLDER
and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/battery-health-center/
Recorded history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/battery-health-center/settings.ini
Preferences.
.TP
.I /etc/battery-health-center.conf
Saved charge limits, re-applied at boot and after sleep.
.TP
.I /etc/battery-health-center.schedule
The charging schedule and optimized charging setting.
.SH AUTHOR
Alexis Rios-Negron.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/arios4k/battery-health-center
